+# Correcting a Booked Visit Narrows NG-5
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 declined both changing and cancelling a booked visit. The [2026-08-08 non-goal ADR](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) confirmed that row as deliberate rather than a survey artifact. It also set the condition for reopening it: an explicit owner decision, recorded at intake, never the request itself.
+
+The owner has now made that decision (2026-08-27). A visit booked with the wrong date or the wrong description has no forward correction path today, while owner and pet details both have one.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-5 whole.** Rejected: the sample corrects owner and pet records forward, and a visit is the one record it cannot correct. The asymmetry teaches nothing about the stack.
+2. **Open the row entirely, cancellation included.** Rejected: cancellation removes a record, which NG-4 excludes, and it introduces the lifecycle state the sample carries nowhere else.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation only** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-5 now covers cancelling a booked visit only. Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope as `REQ-VIS-003`, judged by the same rules as booking. The 2026-08-08 ADR's NG-4 half stands untouched, and so does its rule for future narrowings.
+
+The correction has no entry point on the owner's record in this scope. That omission is a decision, not an oversight; a visible entry point is a separate request.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The sample still removes nothing. Correction stays forward-only, matching how owner and pet records already behave.
+- Cancelling a booked visit remains declined, and reopening it needs its own recorded owner decision.
+- The correction is reachable only by whoever knows where it is until a later request adds a link.
+- Three questions stay open, listed under [Open Questions](../prd.md#open-questions). They ask whether the correction shows earlier visits, whether an already-passed date may be kept, and when a visible entry point arrives.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and its preamble.
+- [REQ-VIS-003](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the correction capability this narrowing admits.
+
+## References
+
+- [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) — the decision this one narrows.
