+## Deferred Risks
+
+Risks a review confirmed as real and left open on purpose. Each names the code it covers and the ADR carrying the reason it stayed open.
+
+### Incidental aggregate binding on nested-resource form handlers
+
+*Raised by the security review of `REQ-VIS-003`, 2026-08-27. Open.*
+
+Five POST handlers accept `Owner` as a bound `@ModelAttribute`. Four of them use it only as the save target for a nested pet or visit, yet request parameters bind onto the whole owner–pet–visit graph. A POST to a pet or visit route carrying `city`, `address`, `firstName`, or `pets[0].name` writes those fields.
+
+| Handler | Source | Role of `Owner` |
+|---|---|---|
+| `VisitController#processNewVisitForm` | `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/owner/VisitController.java` | save target only |
+| `VisitController#processVisitCorrectionForm` | `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/owner/VisitController.java` | save target only |
+| `PetController#processCreationForm` | `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/owner/PetController.java` | save target only |
+| `PetController#processUpdateForm` | `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/owner/PetController.java` | save target only |
+| `OwnerController#processUpdateOwnerForm` | `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/owner/OwnerController.java` | the form's own subject |
+
+**Contained.** The binders disallow `id` and `*.id`, so the graph cannot be repointed at another owner's rows. `Owner`'s bean-validation constraints are enforced before persistence, so stored values stay well-formed. No privilege boundary is crossed while the application has no authentication — the same unauthenticated writes are reachable on the owner-edit and pet-edit routes ([Security Context](#security-context)).
+
+**Open.** A request to a pet or visit route writes owner and pet fields the form never offered. The owner-edit route writes the nested `pets[*]` scalars its own form never offers. `REQ-VIS-003` widened the class by one handler rather than introducing it.
+
+**Proposed remedy.** Bind the aggregate root with `@ModelAttribute(binding = false)` on the four handlers that use it only as a save target. `OwnerController#processUpdateOwnerForm` needs different treatment: the owner is that form's subject, so binding must stay on. The fields that form does not offer — the nested `pets[*]` scalars — are excluded by an explicit `setAllowedFields` allowlist on its binder. The work belongs to a dedicated hardening slice — see [ADR 2026-08-27](adr/2026-08-27-form-binding-hardening-deferred.md).
